@using Demos.Shared.Services
@inject RouteInfoService RouteInfoObj

<PageTitle>Route Info — Blazor Atoms</PageTitle>

<h3>Available Routes</h3>

<p>
    Everything <code>BlazorAtoms.Breadcrumbs</code> can see. It builds its parent-route graph by
    reflecting over the assemblies loaded in <em>this runtime</em>, so a route missing from the list
    below is a route a breadcrumb trail cannot resolve either.
</p>
<p>
    "This runtime" is load-bearing under <code>InteractiveAuto</code>, where the answer legitimately
    differs between passes. Measured in this repo's Auto demo: <strong>63</strong> templates on the
    server pass, <strong>61</strong> once WebAssembly takes over — the two missing are <code>/</code>
    and <code>/Error</code>, which live in the host project rather than <code>.Client</code>, so the
    browser runtime never loads that assembly. The practical consequence: an
    <code>[AtomBreadcrumb]</code> parent chain pointing at a host-only page resolves server-side and
    silently fails to in WebAssembly. Compare a cold load against a reload here to see it.
</p>

<div>Route Templates</div>
<ul>
    @foreach (var route in RouteInfoObj.RoutesTemplates)
    {
        <li>@route</li>
    }
</ul>

<div>Route objects</div>
<ul>
    @foreach (var route in RouteInfoObj.Routes)
    {
        <li>@route</li>
    }
</ul>

<div>Page Types</div>
<ul>
    @foreach (var type in RouteInfoObj.PageTypes)
{
    <li>@type.FullName</li>
}
</ul>
